# Secrets never enter the repo (CLAUDE.md §4). The pattern covers .env.bak.*
# and any other .env.<something> a session leaves behind, because the last time
# .env was tracked, every `git pull` on the Pi silently replaced the house's
# real configuration with the laptop defaults from .env.example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# A dev database is machine-local state, not source. Tracking it meant a
# permanently dirty working tree, a fresh ~1.1MB blob in every commit that
# touched it (sqlite does not delta-compress), and binary conflicts between
# machines that can only be resolved by picking one. Same class of mistake as
# tracking .env. The file itself stays on disk and keeps working.
db.sqlite3
db.sqlite3-journal
/var/alarms/

nginx/certs/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
/logs/
/media/
/staticfiles/
/backups/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# Tailwind build (compiled in Docker, never committed)
node_modules/
static/nora_home/css/nh.css
